This directory contains a QuIDDPro script which simulates a randomly
generated circuit consisting of Toffoli gates and stabilizer gates.  A
program to generate other random circuits of this form is also
included.

The program is called "tsc."  It takes two command-line arguments.
The first argument is the number of desired qubits in the circuit
(must be greater than 2).  The second argument is the number of
desired gates in the circuit.  The generated QuIDDPro script is simply
sent to standard out.  So, to store the generated QuIDDPro script to a
file, redirect standard out to a file.  For example,

./tsc 100 300 > tchp100.qpro

will create a 100-qubit random circuit with 300 gates consisting of
Toffoli gates and stabilizer gates.

Scripts
-------

tchp100.qpro: A 100-qubit random circuit with 300 gates consisting of
             Toffoli gates and stabilizer gates
